public","site_admin":true},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n`.instructions.md` files, designed to provide custom instructions for AI chat and agent functionalities, are not being respected or applied in both VS Code stable and insider builds. This issue prevents users from leveraging predefined instructions for specific tasks, programming languages, frameworks, or project types, leading to repetitive manual instruction input and a degraded user experience for AI-assisted development.\n\nI am trying below example but it's not working.\n\n```markdown\n---\napplyTo: \"**/*.md\"\n---\n\n## Follow below things for Markdown Files\n\n1. Do not use markdown bold (**) and italic (_) formatting in the markdown file. Use only headings, lists, and code blocks.\n2. Also add markdown divider --- after each heading like # or ## or ###.\n```\n\n## Solution\nInvestigate and resolve the bug preventing VS Code's chat and agent features from correctly parsing and applying instructions defined in `.instructions.md` files. This includes ensuring proper recognition of both workspace and user instruction files, correct interpretation of `applyTo` metadata, and consistent application of instruction content across all relevant AI interactions.\n\n## Benefits\n* **Enhanced Productivity:** Users can automate the inclusion of custom AI instructions, saving time and effort.\n* **Consistent AI Behavior:** Ensures AI agents and chat responses adhere to predefined guidelines, improving accuracy and relevance.\n* **Improved User Experience:** Streamlines the interaction with AI features in VS Code, making them more powerful and user-friendly.\n* **Better Customization:** Fully leverages the intended functionality of `.instructions.md` files for tailored AI assistance.","closed_by":{"login":"aeschli","id":6461412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjE0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6461412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli","html_url":"https://github.com/aeschli","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},"comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2986576182","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2986576182","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2986576182,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yA4k2","user":{"login":"beingminimal","id":84431724,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDMxNzI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84431724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal","html_url":"https://github.com/beingminimal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T04:39:10Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T04:39:10Z","body":"Here is video that shows it's not working @digitarald \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e27ecc1f-3a40-45ee-b19d-37d2f0aabba1","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2986576182/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2987772547","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2987772547","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2987772547,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yFcqD","user":{"login":"aeschli","id":6461412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjE0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6461412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli","html_url":"https://github.com/aeschli","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-06-19T11:43:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T11:43:34Z","body":"The automatic inclusion of instructions is currently based on the files that are part of the request context.\nIn your case, there is no context, so no instructions are auto added.\n\nIn this release I added information to the prompt so that the agent can load the instructions when not present and needed.\n\nTBH for now its the best to just mark your instructions as `**`. This will always include them, but given that they are small, this is not a problem. Even with the latest change, this will be more efficient that having the LLM to make a load.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2987772547/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2987790844","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2987790844","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2987790844,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yFhH8","user":{"login":"aeschli","id":6461412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjE0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6461412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli","html_url":"https://github.com/aeschli","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-06-19T11:47:03Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T11:47:03Z","body":"The internal issue where we track this is https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot/issues/17214","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2987790844/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988239812","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2988239812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2988239812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yHOvE","user":{"login":"beingminimal","id":84431724,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDMxNzI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84431724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal","html_url":"https://github.com/beingminimal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T14:09:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T14:09:27Z","body":"> The automatic inclusion of instructions is currently based on the files that are part of the request context. In your case, there is no context, so no instructions are auto added.\n> \n> In this release I added information to the prompt so that the agent can load the instructions when not present and needed.\n> \n> TBH for now its the best to just mark your instructions as `**`. This will always include them, but given that they are small, this is not a problem. Even with the latest change, this will be more efficient that having the LLM to make a load.\n\nSo what i understood is i don't need to give instructions.md file in copilot chat/agent context but only those files on which i want to apply instructions.md files and want to generate code or docs? is this correct?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988239812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988277701","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2988277701","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2988277701,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yHX_F","user":{"login":"aeschli","id":6461412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjE0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6461412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli","html_url":"https://github.com/aeschli","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-06-19T14:21:09Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T14:21:44Z","body":"You can add `.instructions.md` files either manually to the context or let them be added automatically. The automatic addition is based on the files that are attached as context of the request.\n\nIf you want them to be added automatically, you need to define the `applyTo` header:\n- `**`: it will be added to every request\n- `**/*.ts`: it will be added to all requests that have a typescript file attached as context of the request\n- if there's no typescript file attached as context of the request, the instruction will not be added. It won't be present if the LLM decides to create a TypeScript file.\n\nNew in June:\nIf there's no typescript file attached as context, the LLM can load as we give it now the list of all instruction files","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988277701/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988452810","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2988452810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2988452810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yICvK","user":{"login":"beingminimal","id":84431724,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDMxNzI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84431724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal","html_url":"https://github.com/beingminimal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T15:12:22Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T15:12:37Z","body":"> New in June: If there's no typescript file attached as context, the LLM can load as we give it now the list of all instruction files\n\nis it supported in today's insider release or going to be supported in vs code June 2025 release?\n\nThanks a lot for your reply and help.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988452810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988457994","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2988457994","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2988457994,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yIEAK","user":{"login":"beingminimal","id":84431724,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDMxNzI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84431724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal","html_url":"https://github.com/beingminimal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T15:14:36Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T15:14:36Z","body":"@aeschli \n\nCan you please help to confirm this?\n\n**Question 1: Automatic Instruction Application for `.ts` Files in Chat/Agent Mode (Current Support & Future Plans)**\n\nIs it possible **right now** to configure GitHub Copilot in chat/agent mode such that instructions defined with `applyTo: **/*.ts` are automatically applied to *any* `.ts` file being worked on or generated, even if that `.ts` file is not explicitly added to the Copilot chat/agent context? If not currently supported, is there an estimated time of arrival (ETA) for this functionality, or are you considering supporting this in the future?\n\n**Question 2: Custom Mode Support for Instruction Application**\n\nRegarding the custom mode of GitHub Copilot, how will the automatic application of instructions (as described in Question 1) be supported within this custom mode? Are there specific configurations or mechanisms in custom mode that allow for broader, context-independent application of instructions to file types like `.ts`?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2988457994/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2989984353","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2989984353","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2989984353,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yN4ph","user":{"login":"aeschli","id":6461412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NjE0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6461412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli","html_url":"https://github.com/aeschli","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aeschli/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"created_at":"2025-06-20T06:47:53Z","updated_at":"2025-06-23T08:32:57Z","body":"I can only repeat what I wrote above:\nIn May, the automatic inclusion of instructions happens when the request is made and depends on what files are attached at that time\nIn June (and current insiders), we now tell the MML what instruction file there are, and the LLM can decide to load additional instructions. It works well for some models like Sonnet, while other models like gpt 4.1 tend ignore it.\n\nThis is no different for custom modes. If works for all modes that have the `read_file` agent enabled.\n\nWe are still experimenting here. \nAgain, if instructions are short, I recommend to use '**' as pattern and have the instruction always included.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2989984353/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2991216367","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2991216367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2991216367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6ySlbv","user":{"login":"beingminimal","id":84431724,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NDMxNzI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/84431724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal","html_url":"https://github.com/beingminimal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beingminimal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T11:52:58Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T11:52:58Z","body":"> I can only repeat what I wrote above: In May, the automatic inclusion of instructions happens when the request is made and depends on what files are attached at that time In June (and current insiders), we now tell the MML what requests there are, and the LLM can decide to load additional instructions. It works well for some models like Sonnect, while other models like gpt 4.1 ignore it.\n> \n> This is no different for custom modes. If works for all modes that have the `read_file` agent enabled.\n> \n> We are still experimenting here. Again, if instructions are short, I recommend to use '**' as pattern and have the instruction always included.\n\nThanks a lot for your reply and efforts and clarity.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2991216367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2994619490","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770#issuecomment-2994619490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/12770","id":2994619490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOJYd5Dc6yfkRi","user":{"login":"hmorneau","id":5209294,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMDkyOTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5209294?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hmorneau"